# CODEOWNERS - segregation of duties as code
#
# In a bank, ownership is not a courtesy: a change to the ledger must be reviewed by the team
# accountable for the ledger, and a change to the mainframe by the people who understand COBOL.
# This file is how that control is expressed in a repository, and it is what makes a required-review
# branch protection rule mean something specific rather than "someone, anyone".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: the team handles below are PLACEHOLDERS and this file has no effect until they are
# replaced with real GitHub teams or usernames. See follow-up F-04 in docs/plan/STATUS.md.
# The structure is retained because the ownership model is the point, and it maps one-to-one onto
# how a real institution divides accountability for this estate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ownership follows the strata, because the skills follow the strata. The team that can safely
# review a Spring Boot 3 pull request is usually not the team that can safely review a change to a
# COBOL match-merge.

# Default - anything not matched below
*                               @tessera-bank/platform-engineering

# Stratum 0 - the mainframe core (~1995)
# Highest-risk area in the estate: it holds the definitive account balances, and the pool of people
# who can review it is the smallest.
/mainframe/                     @tessera-bank/core-banking-mainframe
/contracts/copybook/            @tessera-bank/core-banking-mainframe

# Stratum 1 - the Java EE monolith (~2011)
/legacy/                        @tessera-bank/customer-systems
/contracts/wsdl/                @tessera-bank/customer-systems
/contracts/xsd/                 @tessera-bank/customer-systems

# Stratum 2 - integration
# Requires literacy in every era at once, which is why it has its own owners.
/integration/                   @tessera-bank/integration-services

# Stratum 3 - the ledger. Money movement.
# Any change here is at minimum a normal change, and touching the posting logic makes it major.
/services/ledger-core/          @tessera-bank/ledger-engineering
/contracts/openapi/             @tessera-bank/ledger-engineering
/contracts/asyncapi/            @tessera-bank/ledger-engineering

/services/payment-engine/       @tessera-bank/payments-engineering

# Stratum 4 - the edge
/edge/api-gateway/              @tessera-bank/platform-engineering
/edge/web-banking/              @tessera-bank/digital-channels
/edge/fraud-scoring/            @tessera-bank/financial-crime

# Batch
/batch/recon/                   @tessera-bank/ledger-engineering @tessera-bank/core-banking-mainframe
/batch/reporting/               @tessera-bank/regulatory-reporting

# Governance, compliance and the plan.
# Changes here alter the rules everyone else works under, so they carry the widest review.
/docs/ways-of-working/          @tessera-bank/engineering-governance
/docs/compliance/               @tessera-bank/engineering-governance @tessera-bank/compliance
/docs/governance/               @tessera-bank/engineering-governance
/docs/plan/                     @tessera-bank/engineering-governance
/CLAUDE.md                      @tessera-bank/engineering-governance
/SECURITY.md                    @tessera-bank/engineering-governance @tessera-bank/security
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @tessera-bank/engineering-governance
